  {
   "text": "Al Capone ruled Chicago, but income tax put him in prison.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 4.58
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1929, seven rival gangsters were murdered, and newspapers named him Public Enemy Number One.",
   "start": 5.48,
   "end": 12.5
  },
  {
   "text": "Agents chose income tax: twenty-two counts of evasion.",
   "start": 13.24,
   "end": 16.76
  },
  {
   "text": "His own admissions became evidence.",
   "start": 17.64,
   "end": 19.28
  },
  {
   "text": "Five convictions, eleven years.",
   "start": 20.2,
   "end": 22.08
  },
  {
   "text": "He served in Atlanta, then Alcatraz.",
   "start": 22.82,
   "end": 24.9
  },
  {
   "text": "He died in 1947.",
   "start": 25.64,
   "end": 26.8
  },
  {
   "text": "Right way to stop him?",
